# Keep the Docker build context small and clean (the Dockerfile only needs src/ + .editorconfig).
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
.git/
.github/
documentation/
*.md
.env

# The client's dependency tree (gh#646). Tens of thousands of files that the image builds from the lockfile
# anyway -- leaving them in the context makes every image build crawl for no benefit.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/

# The image builds its own client stage and COPYs the result to /app/wwwroot (Dockerfile), so a local
# `wwwroot/` -- left behind by the `npm run build` + copy-into-wwwroot dev workflow (AGENTS.md) -- is never an
# input. Left in the build context it is COPYed into the build stage and partly survives dotnet publish's
# default web-SDK wwwroot handling: the client stage's COPY overwrites same-named files but does not delete
# orphaned content-hashed assets from an earlier local build (gh#1090). Scoped to this project rather than a
# bare `wwwroot/`, matching the `.gitignore` entry gh#1088 added.
src/MarqSpec.TradingCopilot.Api/wwwroot/
